{#
    Who carries what.

    A table rather than the page's cards: on the dashboard this is a
    comparison, and rows that share their columns are what a reader can run an
    eye down. The Household page, where each member is the subject rather than
    a line in a list, draws the same figures as cards.

    The card renders nothing at all when `member_shares` is empty, which is the
    answer for a Viewer, for a household of one, and for an ISOLATED instance
    where nobody else's figures may be shown. That decision is
    HouseholdOverviewService's; this only asks whether it was given rows.

    The figures go through the same `spend` macro the metric tiles use, so the
    per-currency rule is the one rule rather than a second reading of it — the
    cells only ask for it at table size rather than tile size.
#}
{% import 'partials/avatar.twig' as avatar %}
{% import 'partials/member_share.twig' as share %}
{% import 'partials/spend.twig' as figure %}

{% if member_shares is not empty %}
    <section class="card">
        <h2>{{ t('dashboard.member_shares') }}</h2>
        <p class="muted">{{ t('dashboard.member_shares_note') }}</p>

        {# Wrapped, like every other table: four columns do not fit a phone. #}
        <div class="table-scroll">
            <table class="table">
                <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th scope="col">{{ t('field.member') }}</th>
                    <th scope="col">{{ t('field.subscriptions') }}</th>
                    <th scope="col" class="numeric">{{ t('field.per_month') }}</th>
                    <th scope="col" class="numeric">{{ t('field.per_year') }}</th>
                </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                {% for row in member_shares %}
                    {% set member = row.member %}
                    <tr>
                        <td>
                            <span class="member-identity">
                                {{ avatar.face(
                                    member.userId,
                                    member.displayName,
                                    member.initials(),
                                    member.hasAvatar,
                                    32
                                ) }}
                                <span class="member-names">
                                    <strong>{{ member.displayName }}</strong>
                                    <span class="hint">{{ role_label(member.role.value) }}</span>
                                </span>
                            </span>
                        </td>
                        {#
                            A withheld row cannot reach this card as things
                            stand — isolation leaves at most one member with
                            figures, and the card is then not drawn at all. It
                            is still written out rather than assumed, because
                            the failure it would otherwise produce is a zero
                            where the truth is "not shown", and that is the one
                            kind of wrong number this screen must never print.
                        #}
                        {% if row.figures_withheld %}
                            <td colspan="3" class="muted">{{ t('household.figures_withheld') }}</td>
                        {% else %}
                            <td>{{ share.count(row) }}</td>
                            {#
                                A member with no recurring spend gets a dash
                                rather than the macro's empty case, which is a
                                sentence written for a tile and reads as an
                                apology in a table cell.
                            #}
                            {% if row.monthly.totals is empty %}
                                <td class="numeric muted num">{{ t('common.none_symbol') }}</td>
                                <td class="numeric muted num">{{ t('common.none_symbol') }}</td>
                            {% else %}
                                <td class="numeric member-figure num">{{ figure.spend(row.monthly, '') }}</td>
                                <td class="numeric member-figure num">{{ figure.spend(row.yearly, '') }}</td>
                            {% endif %}
                        {% endif %}
                    </tr>
                {% endfor %}
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
    </section>
{% endif %}
